 in the  world today to help me relate to her i  was very much an idealist  as i experienced more in life i realized  much like george that one has to be able  to balance their ideology with the  reality of the world around them  once c nation ended o'brien continued to  work in genre tv  however the role she played changed from  idealistic leaders to hardened bad gals  after a season of playing the strong and  compassionate george on z nation  o'brien used her martial arts tone  physicality to embody a different kind  of determined character  in the cw series black lightning an  aeroverse show based on the dc comics  character of the same name she plays  major sarah gray a soldier with the  nefarious american security agency or  asa she's introduced in the third season  as a strong woman for agent o'dell  played by bill duke  when he's injured major grey even takes  over command unlike the character  of george who constantly faced difficult  decisions to put her desire to do good  at odds with the circumstances at hand  major grey's motivations are much  simpler as o'brien told comicbook.com  it's less of me having to take the time  to really get into the emotions of the  character because that's i pretty much  know  i have a mission and i need to  accomplish it the relentless drive to  complete a mission made major grey a  formidable antagonist during o'brien's  run on the show  o'brien completed her trifecta of  playing villainous henchwoman on major  sci-fi tv properties when she was cast  in the marvel series agents of shield as  kimball a member of nathaniel malek's  team  the group is made up of baddies who  slipped past their predestined deaths by  jumping through time and space  and considering that malik was born into  a hydro family you better believe that  one of the main priorities  for this group of time traveling terrors  was to destroy shield  sadly for kimball she put her money on  the wrong megalomaniac horse  a fate she found out when she and the 